# slice_of_union_grouped.tkr — the 9D-T1 (crumb 0019) grouped-type-in-primary-position anchor.
# `[](A | B)` (a slice of the grouped union) parses and each element matches its own branch, while
# `[]A | B` (no parens) keeps the `[]` > `|` precedence: `([]A) | B` — a value of the bare `B`
# alternative is accepted where the slice-of-A/plain-B union is expected.

Feature: slice_of_union_grouped — a grouped inner union in a slice element, and `[]` > `|` precedence

